    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb8a685d_350c44c7",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/android/net/ip/IpServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 355,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T03:10:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think WaitingForRestartState should be a substate of mTetheredState, otherwise you end up calling mTetheredState.exit() which tears down the downstream, then have Tethering stop tethering (which should also attempt to tear down the downstream); so this creates an unusual teardown path that\u0027s not well tested.\n\nYou could just do:\naddState(mTetheredState, mWaitingForRestartState)\nand you also don\u0027t need to handle CMD_TETHER_UNREQUESTED in WaitingForRestartState\n\nAlso that\u0027s assuming that this mechanism is not valid for local hotspot, so the handling of CMD_RESTART_TETHERING should be moved from BaseServingState to TetheredState",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 355,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 355,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "a988ac65e5d645ae50e5dd58dd336e4f4d9bb7a0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cbf3e549_5dd17e89",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/android/net/ip/IpServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 355,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T08:05:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, but we still need to handle CMD_TETHER_UNREQUESTED in WaitingForRestartState because there is no CMD_INTERFACE_DOWN for hotspot off case. Stop wifi tethering would have CMD_TETHER_UNREQUESTED notify IpServer that wifi framework(and driver) is stopped. We also need to handle restart case for this command.",
      "parentUuid": "cb8a685d_350c44c7",
