    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee30b89d_dda1c3d8",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/PrivateAddressCoordinator.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T03:10:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not well protected against races as there is no guarantee here that there won\u0027t be 2 conflicts, so the first one will be lost.\n\nMaybe this can be in another CL, but I think this should implement what we discussed in the meeting yesterday:\n - Keep a set of previously conflicting prefixes and just don\u0027t delete them; except when you start tethering and there\u0027s more than X (like 50)\n - Or (maybe my preference) keep a map of network -\u003e list\u003cprefix\u003e of previously conflicting prefixes, and when you start tethering remove all networks that are not in ConnectivityManager.getAllNetworks()",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 88,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "a988ac65e5d645ae50e5dd58dd336e4f4d9bb7a0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c915582_fcc489f4",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/PrivateAddressCoordinator.java",
